WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:02.084
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:02.086 --> 00:03.669
Can I ask you
a personal question?

00:03.671 --> 00:07.332
No, Jake, I've never
measured my penis.

00:07.333 --> 00:08.700
No, it's not about that.

00:08.702 --> 00:10.851
I heard my dad say you're
worth like a billion dollars.

00:10.853 --> 00:12.970
You know, I'm not
really comfortable

00:12.972 --> 00:14.789
talking about my
financial situation.

00:14.791 --> 00:16.074
Oh, okay.

00:16.076 --> 00:18.323
Let's just say I'd have
more money than God,

00:18.348 --> 00:20.515
if God only had 900 million.

00:22.233 --> 00:24.423
Wow! You don't have any kids,
do you?

00:24.469 --> 00:28.338
- Nope.
- Here, let me push the cart.

00:28.340 --> 00:30.641
Thanks. So if you have
so much money,

00:30.643 --> 00:32.292
why do you do your
own grocery shopping?

00:32.294 --> 00:33.727
I mean, you could
just write a list

00:33.729 --> 00:35.345
and hire someone
to do it for you.

00:35.347 --> 00:36.730
You know, like a
17-year-old go-getter

00:36.732 --> 00:37.898
with a valid driver's license

00:37.900 --> 00:39.466
and no chance at
getting into college?

00:39.468 --> 00:43.687
Well, I could, but you know,
since I've been single

00:43.689 --> 00:46.106
I find I really like
shopping for myself.

00:46.108 --> 00:47.741
You're kidding. Why?

00:47.743 --> 00:50.160
Well, take this, for example.

00:50.162 --> 00:52.863
"Baco-berries." How could
I put this on a list?

00:52.865 --> 00:55.148
I didn't even
know it existed.

00:55.150 --> 00:56.616
I don't even know
what it is.

00:56.618 --> 00:58.001
What is it, anyway?

00:58.003 --> 01:02.773
"Delicious dried cranberries
infused with real bacon flavor""

01:02.775 --> 01:04.958
Ugh, that's disgusting.

01:09.681 --> 01:12.632
So... do you have a bunch of
houses and yachts and stuff?

01:12.634 --> 01:15.052
Two houses, no yachts.

01:15.054 --> 01:16.803
You should totally get a yacht,

01:16.805 --> 01:18.689
and then hire someone
to drive it for you.

01:18.691 --> 01:20.357
You know, like
a 17-year-old go-getter

01:20.359 --> 01:22.192
with a valid yacht
driver's license.

01:22.194 --> 01:24.144
Ah, yachts are pretentious.

01:24.146 --> 01:26.679
I don't believe in ostentatious
displays of wealth.

01:26.681 --> 01:28.181
Besides, if I need
to get anywhere,

01:28.183 --> 01:30.350
I'll just take my private jet.

01:30.352 --> 01:32.018
You have a jet?

01:32.020 --> 01:33.537
Yeah, and I already got
a go-getter pilot.

01:33.539 --> 01:34.988
With a college degree.

01:36.240 --> 01:38.959
Excuse me, do you know
the difference

01:38.961 --> 01:41.161
between "organic beef"
and "grass-fed beef"?

01:41.163 --> 01:44.998
Yeah, "organic" is, uh, no
antibiotics or growth hormones,

01:45.000 --> 01:46.833
but it can still be
force-fed grain, which produces

01:46.835 --> 01:48.752
a less nutritious product
than cows that are allowed

01:48.754 --> 01:50.170
to naturally graze on grass.

01:50.172 --> 01:51.855
Speaking of which,
you're very pretty,

01:51.857 --> 01:53.790
and your accent makes me
feel tingly inside.

01:53.792 --> 01:56.510
Speaking of which...?

01:56.512 --> 01:58.178
Cows, meat, cuts of steak,

01:58.180 --> 02:00.263
London Broil, England,
your accent,

02:00.265 --> 02:01.515
'ello!

02:02.517 --> 02:04.651
- Hello. I'm Zoey.
- Walden.

02:04.653 --> 02:06.686
Nice to meet you, Walden.

02:06.688 --> 02:09.239
Your accent's rather
charming, as well.

02:09.241 --> 02:10.290
Thanks.

02:11.993 --> 02:14.161
Good luck with your meat.

02:14.163 --> 02:16.696
Thanks.

02:18.666 --> 02:21.001
And they call me Forrest Gump.

02:21.003 --> 02:22.735
What?

02:22.737 --> 02:24.737
She was totally hitting on you.

02:24.739 --> 02:26.006
Really?

02:26.008 --> 02:27.257
You should ask her out.

02:27.259 --> 02:29.543
Okay.

02:29.545 --> 02:31.878
Hey, Zoey, you want to
go on a date with me?

02:31.880 --> 02:33.930
Sure!

02:33.932 --> 02:35.081
See, there's something else

02:35.083 --> 02:36.850
I wouldn't know to
put on the list.

02:38.018 --> 02:42.018
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x10 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">A Fishbowl Full of Glass Eyes&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on November 21, 2011

02:42.019 --> 02:46.019
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

02:47.295 --> 02:49.446
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

02:49.448 --> 02:51.215
Okay...

02:51.217 --> 02:56.053
I can pay the Mastercard
with the Visa,

02:56.055 --> 03:00.975
and the Visa
with the Discover card,

03:00.977 --> 03:06.147
and the Discover with
the American Express...

03:06.149 --> 03:10.401
Now what can I use to complete
my little Ponzi scheme?

03:12.687 --> 03:14.655
Chevron? No.

03:14.657 --> 03:18.025
Blockbuster? They're in
worse shape than I am.

03:18.027 --> 03:19.860
Starbucks gift card.

03:19.862 --> 03:21.829
Ooh, hello latte!

03:21.831 --> 03:23.814
- Hey.
- Hey.

03:23.816 --> 03:25.666
Oh, I know that game--

03:25.668 --> 03:28.169
"Seven Card Screwed."

03:28.171 --> 03:30.871
If I could just get
a little ahead, I'd be fine.

03:30.873 --> 03:32.227
And if I could just
lose a little weight,

03:32.228 --> 03:33.611
I'd be a swimsuit model.

03:34.677 --> 03:37.845
Go ahead, say something,
I dare you.

03:37.847 --> 03:40.848
Oh, no, no.
It's an apt comparison.

03:40.850 --> 03:42.933
They both involve
losing your ass.

03:46.404 --> 03:48.222
Well, I hate to do it,

03:48.224 --> 03:50.674
but I-I could ask Walden
for a short-term loan.

03:50.676 --> 03:53.561
For God's sakes, Zippy,
the man is already

03:53.563 --> 03:56.013
letting you and your kid
live here rent-free.

03:56.015 --> 03:57.898
Don't you have
any pride at all?

03:58.733 --> 04:01.569
Let me say that another way.

04:02.637 --> 04:05.322
Why do you think he's
letting you stay here?

04:05.324 --> 04:06.657
Because he likes me.

04:06.659 --> 04:09.210
Because he likes having at
least one person in his life

04:09.212 --> 04:11.695
that doesn't want
anything from him.

04:11.697 --> 04:14.164
Somebody he thinks
cares about him as a person.

04:14.166 --> 04:15.749
That's a good point.

04:15.751 --> 04:17.551
What you don't
want him to find out

04:17.553 --> 04:19.637
is that you're just one of
those nasty little birds

04:19.639 --> 04:23.007
that picks the food
out of a hippo's teeth.

04:24.676 --> 04:26.844
No, we don't want that.

04:28.263 --> 04:30.380
So, listen, uh...

04:30.382 --> 04:31.932
I suppose, over the years,

04:31.934 --> 04:34.101
you've salted away
a pretty good nest egg.

04:34.103 --> 04:36.553
You're not going to
ask me for money.

04:36.555 --> 04:38.522
No, no! Just making
conversation.

04:39.941 --> 04:41.909
Thanks for bringing in
my groceries, man.

04:41.911 --> 04:42.977
I live to serve.

04:42.979 --> 04:45.329
Boy, I gotta
tell you, Alan,

04:45.331 --> 04:47.831
your son made one heck of
a wingman today.

04:47.833 --> 04:49.450
You make it easy, boss.

04:50.919 --> 04:54.171
Baby bird doesn't fly far
from the teeth.

04:55.757 --> 04:57.124
So you, uh, you met somebody?

04:57.126 --> 04:58.842
Indeed I did.

04:58.844 --> 05:00.294
Beautiful woman. British.

05:00.296 --> 05:03.547
Actually drove her shopping cart
on the wrong side of the aisle.

05:03.549 --> 05:05.716
That's a lot of credit cards.

05:05.718 --> 05:06.800
Uh, yeah.

05:06.802 --> 05:08.602
I've only got this
one black one.

05:08.604 --> 05:10.354
I actually bought
my plane with it.

05:10.356 --> 05:12.139
Oh, oh, oh!
Which reminds me.

05:12.141 --> 05:14.058
Hey Jake, you want
a quarter of a million

05:14.060 --> 05:16.310
frequent flyer miles? I can't
use 'em, I got a plane.

05:16.312 --> 05:18.479
I want a quarter of
a million anything.

05:19.114 --> 05:21.031
All yours, my man.

05:21.033 --> 05:24.401
Hmm, where could I go that's a
quarter of a million miles away?

05:24.403 --> 05:25.986
How about the moon?

05:25.988 --> 05:27.655
That's ridiculous, Dad.

05:27.657 --> 05:29.206
I know, I was kidding.

05:29.208 --> 05:31.292
No one's ever been to the moon.

05:33.628 --> 05:35.913
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

05:36.581 --> 05:38.382
Here you go.

05:38.384 --> 05:40.884
State of the art.

05:40.886 --> 05:43.053
And semi-portable.

05:43.055 --> 05:44.888
Gateway computer.

05:44.890 --> 05:46.724
I haven't seen one
of these in a while.

05:46.726 --> 05:49.310
Still works great. And it
is loaded with software.

05:49.312 --> 05:55.432
Quicken 95, Lotus 1-2-3...
um... WordPerfect, Tetris.

05:55.434 --> 05:57.300
I don't know, pal.

05:57.302 --> 05:58.652
I don't think I can move this.

05:58.654 --> 06:00.521
Oh, come on, help me out,
I'm desperate.

06:00.523 --> 06:03.807
As opposed to most of
the people who come in here.

06:03.809 --> 06:07.161
In my storeroom, I've got
a couple of wheelchairs,

06:07.163 --> 06:09.246
a fishbowl full of glass eyes,

06:09.248 --> 06:10.948
and a "boy in the bubble" bag.

06:10.950 --> 06:14.618
To be clear, they took
the boy out of the bubble

06:14.620 --> 06:16.453
and sold me the bag.

06:16.455 --> 06:18.288
Um...

06:18.290 --> 06:21.625
Uh, what would you give me for
a pair of diamond cufflinks?

06:21.627 --> 06:24.461
Oh...

06:24.463 --> 06:26.663
Where'd you get these?

06:26.665 --> 06:29.216
My mother gave them to me
when I graduated college.

06:29.218 --> 06:31.352
- Is she your real mother?
- Yeah. Why?

06:31.354 --> 06:33.937
'Cause these aren't
real diamonds.

06:34.756 --> 06:36.023
What?!

06:36.025 --> 06:38.842
I'm sure she was a good
mother in other ways.

06:38.844 --> 06:41.395
No, this is the nicest thing
she ever did for me.

06:41.397 --> 06:43.030
I'm very sorry.

06:43.032 --> 06:46.516
All right. All right. I didn't
want to have to sell this,

06:46.518 --> 06:49.286
but, uh, I suppose
I'm out of options.

06:49.288 --> 06:50.971
Ooh.

06:50.973 --> 06:54.408
Oh, nice.

06:54.410 --> 06:56.293
Steuben crystal, huh?

06:56.295 --> 06:57.444
It is.

06:57.446 --> 07:00.748
Your mother didn't
give you this.

07:00.750 --> 07:02.783
No. It was a wedding gift
from my wife's parents.

07:02.785 --> 07:05.368
I managed to sneak it out of
the house after the divorce.

07:05.370 --> 07:07.671
Uh-huh. Well, gimme a sec.

07:09.540 --> 07:12.342
I'll give you $1,200.

07:12.344 --> 07:14.377
Yes!

07:14.379 --> 07:16.546
No!

07:21.302 --> 07:24.438
I'll give you $2.00
to clean it up.

07:25.273 --> 07:28.225
Where's your broom?

07:28.227 --> 07:30.527
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

07:32.030 --> 07:33.530
Jake, I'm ready to go!

07:33.532 --> 07:36.200
Coming!

07:36.202 --> 07:38.068
Here you go, sir.
The car is charged, washed,

07:38.070 --> 07:39.920
and I put an air freshener
under your seat

07:39.922 --> 07:42.206
just in case you
let one slip out.

07:43.291 --> 07:44.341
Good job.

07:44.343 --> 07:46.543
Hundred bucks! Thanks, boss.

07:49.931 --> 07:51.932
You gave him $100?

07:51.934 --> 07:54.301
Oh, hey, Alan.
Yeah, he washed my car.

07:54.303 --> 07:56.553
A hundred bucks
to wash a car?

07:56.555 --> 07:58.088
Not enough?

07:58.090 --> 08:01.225
For $100,
I'd &lt;i>lick&lt;/i> your car clean.

08:01.227 --> 08:03.143
Maybe next time.

08:04.813 --> 08:06.447
Hey, I'm going on
a date with that girl

08:06.449 --> 08:08.232
I met in at supermarket.
Do I look okay?

08:08.234 --> 08:09.432
No, I look okay.

08:09.434 --> 08:11.318
You look like the guy
women fantasize about

08:11.320 --> 08:13.153
when I'm on top of them.

08:14.989 --> 08:18.608
Listen, I-I know you're still
pretty new to the dating world,

08:18.610 --> 08:20.294
but can I give you
a little advice?

08:20.296 --> 08:21.444
Is this about condoms?

08:21.446 --> 08:23.163
'Cause Jake already
gave me his lucky one.

08:24.999 --> 08:27.117
No. Uh...

08:27.119 --> 08:29.619
If you hope to have any
kind of shot with this woman,

08:29.621 --> 08:31.588
you, uh, might want to
lose the wedding ring.

08:31.590 --> 08:33.340
Really?

08:33.342 --> 08:34.341
Oh yeah.

08:34.343 --> 08:36.143
When it comes to dating,

08:36.145 --> 08:38.128
wedding rings are
like kryptonite.

08:38.130 --> 08:42.766
If, you know,
Superman was a... vagina.

08:45.469 --> 08:47.321
You know, I haven't
taken this off in years.

08:47.323 --> 08:50.941
When Bridget and I first got
together, we were pretty broke,

08:50.943 --> 08:53.476
so we just exchanged
these cheap bands,

08:53.478 --> 08:55.979
but then, after I made my first
million, I got matching ones

08:55.981 --> 08:58.648
made out of rhodium
and platinum.

08:58.650 --> 09:02.202
In retrospect, I should've had
them made out of poop and tears.

09:02.204 --> 09:05.172
Wait, uh... what's rhodium?

09:05.174 --> 09:06.924
It's the most expensive
metal in the world.

09:06.926 --> 09:08.876
To symbolize how precious
our love was.

09:08.878 --> 09:10.961
Well, that's... very romantic.

09:10.963 --> 09:13.797
But again, it's Lex Luthor
for lady parts.

09:14.632 --> 09:16.850
Boy...

09:16.852 --> 09:18.302
This is gonna be tough.

09:19.938 --> 09:22.356
Wearing it makes me feel...

09:22.358 --> 09:24.525
secure.

09:24.527 --> 09:28.011
Be that as it may,
you have a choice to make.

09:28.013 --> 09:30.847
Either the past,
or the future.

09:30.849 --> 09:34.034
The memory of Bridget,
or the promise of...

09:34.036 --> 09:37.037
supermarket strange.

09:40.325 --> 09:42.709
- Here.
- Why are you giving it to me?

09:42.711 --> 09:43.744
Because you're right.

09:43.746 --> 09:45.528
I've got to
move on with my life.

09:45.530 --> 09:47.998
And this ring is just an anchor
chaining me to the past.

09:48.000 --> 09:49.082
Thanks, Al.

09:49.084 --> 09:51.752
Well, you are very welcome.
Enjoy your date!

09:51.754 --> 09:53.804
Will do. See you.

09:55.707 --> 09:57.591
My precious!

09:57.593 --> 09:59.226
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:05.227 --> 10:07.034
So the young man you were
with at the supermarket

10:07.035 --> 10:08.034
is no relation to you?

10:08.036 --> 10:09.920
Oh, no, Jake...
Mm.

10:09.922 --> 10:11.972
is Alan's son.

10:11.974 --> 10:14.308
And Alan is...?

10:14.310 --> 10:17.010
Uh, it's complicated.

10:17.845 --> 10:20.097
I'm fairly bright, try me.

10:20.099 --> 10:22.549
Okay.

10:22.551 --> 10:25.552
Um, when I tried to kill
myself in the ocean,

10:25.554 --> 10:28.188
Alan's house was
the closest one with a phone.

10:30.057 --> 10:31.325
I see.

10:31.327 --> 10:33.961
- You don't, do you?
- Not at all.

10:33.963 --> 10:36.780
- Okay, let me back up.
- Please do.

10:36.782 --> 10:40.117
Okay, when I was in high school,
I met this girl named Bridget.

10:40.119 --> 10:42.869
Is it really necessary to
back up quite that far?

10:42.871 --> 10:45.905
You're right, I'll skip ahead.

10:45.907 --> 10:48.925
Let's see... I got married
right after high school,

10:48.927 --> 10:50.243
happy, happy, happy.

10:50.245 --> 10:52.245
Made like a billion dollars,
rich, rich, rich.

10:52.247 --> 10:54.214
She decided she didn't
want to be married anymore,

10:54.216 --> 10:55.248
sad, sad, sad.

10:55.250 --> 10:56.683
In the ocean,
out of the ocean,

10:56.685 --> 11:00.020
bought Alan's house, got rid
of the furniture, kept Alan,

11:00.022 --> 11:03.640
got hungry, went to the
supermarket, met you. The end.

11:04.976 --> 11:06.727
Wow.

11:06.729 --> 11:08.312
Enough about me.
Let's talk about you.

11:08.314 --> 11:10.814
No, no, I have a few
follow-up questions.

11:10.816 --> 11:11.898
The furniture?

11:11.900 --> 11:13.367
The suicide.

11:13.369 --> 11:16.570
Oh, it was just a cry
for attention.

11:16.572 --> 11:18.405
I wanted Bridget
to feel sorry for me.

11:18.407 --> 11:20.824
Well, that's rather pathetic.

11:20.826 --> 11:23.043
In hindsight, yeah.

11:23.745 --> 11:25.278
And the billion dollars?

11:25.280 --> 11:27.998
I sold a couple companies
to Microsoft.

11:28.000 --> 11:29.166
Big mistake.

11:29.168 --> 11:30.584
Oh, you regret it?

11:30.586 --> 11:32.886
No, they do.

11:34.622 --> 11:36.473
How long's it been
since your wife left?

11:36.475 --> 11:40.594
Four months, three weeks,
four days, six hours and change.

11:41.646 --> 11:44.064
Let's just call it six hours.

11:44.066 --> 11:46.900
You're still in love
with her, aren't you?

11:49.554 --> 11:51.104
You really &lt;i>are&lt;/i> bright.

11:52.156 --> 11:53.874
I thought it was
just your accent.

11:53.876 --> 11:55.325
It kind of raises
the question,

11:55.327 --> 11:57.411
"Why on Earth did
you ask me out""

11:57.413 --> 11:58.745
Jake told me to.

11:58.747 --> 12:00.864
Alan's son.

12:00.866 --> 12:05.202
Yeah, and also wanted to because
I'm moving on with my life.

12:05.204 --> 12:06.503
See? Look, no wedding ring.

12:06.505 --> 12:08.672
Mmm, I noticed the
bright white tan line.

12:08.674 --> 12:11.091
Yeah, it's almost like
I still got it on.

12:11.093 --> 12:12.776
It is.

12:12.778 --> 12:14.711
No worries. I gave it to Alan.

12:14.713 --> 12:17.714
The man you kept
instead of furniture.

12:17.716 --> 12:20.133
Well, it wasn't an either/or.

12:21.719 --> 12:23.053
What about you?
What's your deal?

12:23.055 --> 12:25.439
My deal.

12:25.441 --> 12:27.023
All right, I'm a lawyer.

12:27.025 --> 12:28.725
Ugh! Ech!

12:30.845 --> 12:31.978
What else?

12:31.980 --> 12:34.648
Well, I'm divorced and I have

12:34.650 --> 12:36.700
a five-year-old daughter, Ava.

12:36.702 --> 12:38.151
I always wanted to have kids,

12:38.153 --> 12:40.353
but Bridget insisted
that we already had one.

12:40.355 --> 12:41.738
I don't follow.

12:41.740 --> 12:42.906
Me.

12:42.908 --> 12:45.525
Oh, sure, I can see that.

12:48.413 --> 12:50.046
What do you think?

12:50.048 --> 12:52.382
Are we gonna fall in love
and stuff?

12:54.135 --> 12:55.385
What?

12:55.387 --> 12:58.305
'Cause that would really teach
Bridget a lesson.

13:02.026 --> 13:03.143
Hi, again.

13:03.145 --> 13:06.096
Oy gevalt.

13:06.098 --> 13:08.732
I, uh, brought something
else for you.

13:08.734 --> 13:12.402
My sphincter's tight
with anticipation.

13:12.404 --> 13:15.188
Platinum and rhodium.

13:15.740 --> 13:17.474
Whoa.

13:19.193 --> 13:22.228
Oh...

13:22.230 --> 13:23.997
very valuable.

13:23.999 --> 13:25.615
Did you steal it?

13:25.617 --> 13:27.017
What?

13:27.019 --> 13:31.872
I'm only asking because it
affects my marketing strategy.

13:31.874 --> 13:33.673
No, it was a gift.

13:33.675 --> 13:34.841
A gift.

13:34.843 --> 13:35.625
Mmm-hmm.

13:35.627 --> 13:38.578
Heh. Good enough for me.

13:38.580 --> 13:41.097
What are you
looking to get for it?

13:41.099 --> 13:42.582
Let's not play this game.

13:42.584 --> 13:44.968
Just... just tell me
what it's worth to you.

13:50.942 --> 13:53.927
What is this,
your phone number?

13:53.929 --> 13:55.278
That's my offer.

14:00.768 --> 14:01.985
Hang on a sec.

14:06.958 --> 14:08.742
You know that's helium?

14:08.744 --> 14:09.743
Hmm?

14:09.745 --> 14:12.629
A down-on-his-luck
birthday clown.

14:12.631 --> 14:16.166
Son of a bitch!

14:16.168 --> 14:17.918
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

14:18.669 --> 14:20.136
This was a lovely
evening, Walden.

14:20.138 --> 14:21.087
Thank you.

14:21.089 --> 14:22.055
You're welcome.

14:22.057 --> 14:24.724
Hmm. Well, better

14:24.726 --> 14:26.726
get in, let Ava's
babysitter go home.

14:26.728 --> 14:28.294
Oh, is she still up?
Can I meet her?

14:28.296 --> 14:30.597
I'm sure she's still up,
but no.

14:30.599 --> 14:33.183
Oh, I get it.

14:33.185 --> 14:35.685
You want to know make
sure a guy's gonna be

14:35.687 --> 14:37.804
around a while before
you introduce him-- me.

14:37.806 --> 14:40.023
Exactly.

14:40.025 --> 14:41.908
So, maybe after the third
or fourth date?

14:41.910 --> 14:43.193
I don't think so.

14:43.195 --> 14:44.644
Well, the fifth or sixth?

14:44.646 --> 14:46.029
No.

14:46.031 --> 14:47.797
Seventh or eighth?

14:49.867 --> 14:52.452
I'm starting
to get a bad feeling.

14:52.454 --> 14:55.755
Oh, I'm sorry.

14:55.757 --> 14:57.657
You seem
like a really sweet guy,

14:57.659 --> 15:00.660
but I think you're still kind
of married to your Bridget.

15:00.662 --> 15:02.429
No, no, I'm not.

15:02.431 --> 15:04.514
I haven't been wearing
my ring for, like,

15:04.516 --> 15:06.266
like, almost three hours now.

15:06.268 --> 15:09.502
It may be off your finger,
but it's still in your head.

15:10.504 --> 15:14.507
Face it, you're not
ready to be dating yet.

15:14.509 --> 15:16.776
Thanks again for dinner.

15:20.197 --> 15:23.400
Still married.

15:23.402 --> 15:25.652
That is so untrue.

15:27.838 --> 15:31.041
Bridget, you're not gonna
believe what just happened.

15:31.742 --> 15:33.843
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:38.365 --> 15:39.716
Walden?

15:51.345 --> 15:52.211
Walden?!

15:52.213 --> 15:54.214
Down here!

16:01.672 --> 16:03.440
Hey.

16:03.442 --> 16:05.224
Hey.

16:05.226 --> 16:06.225
How's your date?

16:06.227 --> 16:07.911
Not so good.

16:07.913 --> 16:11.281
Oh. So much for Jake's
lucky condom, huh?

16:11.283 --> 16:13.900
Yeah, we never got
to condoms.

16:15.369 --> 16:18.237
She thinks I'm still too
hung up on Bridget.

16:18.239 --> 16:19.873
No kidding.

16:19.875 --> 16:22.342
And the worst part is
Bridget agrees with her.

16:24.178 --> 16:28.381
Well, I might as well put
my ring back on.

16:31.052 --> 16:34.387
You, uh, you, uh, want-want
your ring back?

16:34.389 --> 16:35.755
Yeah.

16:38.442 --> 16:39.776
Here.

16:39.778 --> 16:42.095
Thanks.

16:43.397 --> 16:46.566
I had a feeling sooner
or later you'd want it.

16:48.819 --> 16:52.322
No. You know what?
I was right the first time.

16:52.324 --> 16:53.823
I don't need this anymore.

16:53.825 --> 16:55.875
Are you sure?

16:55.877 --> 16:56.993
I'm positive.

17:02.718 --> 17:04.918
I feel better already.

17:04.920 --> 17:07.303
Oh, good.

17:08.806 --> 17:10.507
All right, I'm gonna
go inside.

17:10.509 --> 17:13.126
Okay, I'm just, I'm just
gonna hang here for a while.

17:13.128 --> 17:14.394
Okay. Good night.

17:14.396 --> 17:16.262
Yeah. Night.

17:19.483 --> 17:22.936
My precious! My precious!
My precious!

17:25.690 --> 17:28.474
My precious! My precious!

17:31.362 --> 17:32.812
My precious!

17:44.022 --> 17:45.384
You saw that?

17:45.385 --> 17:46.551
Yeah.

17:46.553 --> 17:49.987
Probably wondering what it was
all about.

17:49.989 --> 17:51.939
Kinda.

17:51.941 --> 17:55.526
Well... I often enjoy

17:55.528 --> 17:58.162
a, uh, brisk moonlight swim.

17:58.164 --> 17:59.714
Fully clothed?

17:59.716 --> 18:02.533
You leave your clothes on
the beach,

18:02.535 --> 18:06.087
a drifter... steals 'em.

18:06.089 --> 18:07.505
Alan...

18:07.507 --> 18:10.541
I was trying to get
your ring back.

18:10.543 --> 18:12.009
But I don't want it back.

18:12.011 --> 18:13.844
No, not-not for you.

18:13.846 --> 18:15.079
Um, for me.

18:16.348 --> 18:18.549
I was gonna pawn it.

18:18.551 --> 18:19.517
Why?

18:19.519 --> 18:22.553
What do you mean, why?
I need money.

18:22.555 --> 18:24.555
I can't possibly produce enough
sperm and blood

18:24.557 --> 18:26.857
to get out of the hole I'm in.

18:28.593 --> 18:30.311
In fact, I went to the pawn shop

18:30.313 --> 18:31.562
while you were on your date.

18:31.564 --> 18:32.897
But you didn't pawn it.

18:32.899 --> 18:35.399
I couldn't.

18:36.985 --> 18:38.536
Wow, you must have been
freaking out

18:38.538 --> 18:40.204
when I threw it
in the ocean, huh?

18:40.206 --> 18:44.041
The truth of that stands
dripping before you.

18:44.043 --> 18:45.910
Listen, if you
needed money,

18:45.912 --> 18:47.245
why didn't you just ask?

18:47.247 --> 18:49.830
You'd lend me money
if I just asked?

18:49.832 --> 18:51.582
No. I don't believe in
lending money.

18:51.584 --> 18:52.800
I just give it away.

18:52.802 --> 18:55.419
Give it away?

18:55.421 --> 18:57.838
Yeah, I think it's a bad idea
to lend people money.

18:57.840 --> 18:58.923
They never pay you back,

18:58.925 --> 19:00.675
and then you just end up
resenting them.

19:00.677 --> 19:01.842
So how much do you need?

19:01.844 --> 19:05.563
Uh...

19:05.565 --> 19:07.298
No, no, I can't, I can't
take your money.

19:07.300 --> 19:09.517
What, you're too proud?

19:09.519 --> 19:11.652
Oh, God, no, I-I-I
haven't had any pride

19:11.654 --> 19:14.939
since the gym showers
in seventh grade.

19:14.941 --> 19:17.325
No, no, if I took your money,

19:17.327 --> 19:18.943
that would change
our relationship,

19:18.945 --> 19:20.311
and I don't want that.

19:20.313 --> 19:23.247
I want you to think of me as
a friend and not a freeloader.

19:23.249 --> 19:26.450
You don't think that ship's
already sailed?

19:27.786 --> 19:30.538
Allow me at least
the illusion of self-respect.

19:30.540 --> 19:33.624
Would it help your self-respect
if I started charging you rent?

19:33.626 --> 19:36.160
Actually, it would.

19:36.162 --> 19:37.828
Consider it done.

19:37.830 --> 19:40.164
Great.

19:40.166 --> 19:42.717
Oh, I'm gonna be late
this month.

19:42.719 --> 19:44.335
No problem.

19:44.337 --> 19:46.103
Probably next month, too.

19:46.105 --> 19:47.405
Thanks for the heads up.

19:47.407 --> 19:50.441
Okay. I guess I better
go dry off.

19:50.443 --> 19:53.444
Hey, Alan.
Yeah?

19:56.648 --> 19:57.698
You're a quality guy.

19:57.700 --> 19:59.450
Really?

19:59.452 --> 20:02.119
I have a lot of people that
say they're my friend,

20:02.121 --> 20:03.904
but you really are one.

20:03.906 --> 20:06.157
Well, thanks.

20:08.160 --> 20:14.131
Just-just out of curiosity,
if I had asked for, say,

20:14.133 --> 20:16.300
a hundred thousand dollars,

20:16.302 --> 20:19.670
would you have given it to me?

20:19.672 --> 20:21.672
Absolutely.

20:28.647 --> 20:29.730
Where you going?

20:29.732 --> 20:31.882
Back in the ocean.

20:43.061 --> 20:45.079
Hello?

20:45.081 --> 20:47.331
Oh, hey, Jake.

20:47.333 --> 20:51.068
No, your dad's kind of busy
right now.

20:52.454 --> 20:53.704
What's up?

20:53.706 --> 20:56.424
Oh, you used the
frequent flier miles?

20:56.426 --> 20:58.342
That's great.
Where are you?

20:58.344 --> 21:00.378
I have no idea.

21:00.380 --> 21:04.380
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

21:04.600 --> 21:07.468
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪
